delta-period-every-width
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
The open question of canon-documents (the period at widths that are not powers of two), the author: "look up two cubed measurement of two prime gap for that", I-189. Over GF(2) minus is plus, so the sum of two cubes is x^3 + 1 = (x + 1)(x^2 + x + 1), and a width W = 2^k m (m odd) factors as x^W + 1 = (x^m + 1)^(2^k). Predicted from it: at x^2 + x + 1 (x^3 = 1) the law is x + 1 + x^(W-2), which is 1 whenever 3 divides W, so the cube factor adds nothing to the period. Measured by zak period at every byte width 16 to 256 (in/ak/period; host and guest agree): m = 1, period 2^(k-1) (16: 8 ... 256: 128); m = 3, period 2^k (24: 8, 48: 16, 96: 32, 192: 64), the prediction holding; m = 5, 7, 15, period the width itself (40, 56, 80, 112, 120, 160, 224, 240); other m, an odd part dividing 2^ord - 1, ord the order of 2 modulo m (m = 11: 8 x 1023; 17: 8 x 255; 9: 8 x 63; 13: 8 x 315). Wherever L returns, the constant drops out with it, so every state returns. Widths 200, 216, 232, 248 do not return within 65,536 steps: open. Related records: core.test.ts (period(2, 7) = 3, period(2, 73) = 9, 7 x 73 = 2^9 - 1), I-194 and I-200 (511 = 2^9 - 1 = 7 x 73, E7), I-189 (the two cubes, the difference of squares measuring a gap), I-195 and Delta16HasExactPeriodEight.v (period 8 at 16 bits, in Coq).

delta-order-every-width
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The four widths stepping could not reach, the author: "yes lets find it". zak order: L is multiplication by x + x^3 + x^(W-2) modulo x^W + 1; at W = 2^k m its order divides 2^k (2^o - 1), o the order of 2 modulo m, so L is raised to that by squaring and each prime taken out while L^(N/p) stays 1, the constant carried in the same doubling. It agrees with every width zak period settled, in Plan 9 (in/ak/order). The four: width 200 (m = 25) returns in 8 x (2^20 - 1); 216 (m = 27) in 8 x (2^18 - 1)/3; 232 (m = 29) in 715,827,880 = 8 x (2^28 - 1)/3, which 29 divides, so all five of the exceptional set's members divide their widths' periods (five-in-the-period); the constant drops out in each. Width 248 (m = 31) never returns: there L is no unit, rank 243 of 248, so the law merges 32 states into each image and is no permutation; it is the only byte width from 16 to 256 where that happens. 31 = 2^5 - 1, and 2 has order 5 modulo 31.

